WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.700
With entry into the Kalos League driving Ash forward,

2
00:00:04.766 --> 00:00:09.466
our heroes now head to Cyllage City, home of Ash’s next Kalos Gym battle.

3
00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:14.666
If we don’t hurry, we won’t get to the Pokémon Center before the sun sets.

4
00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:17.300
Then we’ll just camp out. No big deal.

5
00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:18.466
We’ll camp out?

6
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.666
- What’s wrong?
- Don’t you have your gear?

7
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:25.433
Well, actually, my mom told me this might happen,

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.966
but I never really considered that I’d end up having to sleep outside for real.

9
00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.000
I brought an extra sleeping bag with me,

10
00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:34.066
so you’re welcome to use it if you'd like.

11
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.000
- And you can sleep with me in my tent.
- Pikachu.

12
00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:40.000
Ah, that’s so nice.

13
00:00:40.066 --> 00:00:42.666
Everybody ready to have a big dinner?

14
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:49.566
Wow, what a feast! Everything looks so totally delicious.

15
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:51.766
Help yourselves. Bon appétit.

16
00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:01.466
It’s great. You’re really a great cook.

17
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:03.833
Thanks. Cooking’s a lot like inventing.

18
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.366
Make a plan, gather materials and then go.

19
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.733
My big brother, the chef. Hooray!

20
00:01:09.966 --> 00:01:13.333
Mm, that was wonderful. Thanks so much.

21
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.733
Yeah, thanks.

22
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.733
- Oh, yeah, am I stuffed.
- Pika.

23
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.333
Now, who has room for dessert?

24
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.733
Yesterday when we stayed at the Pokémon Center, I made macaroons.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.833
- Nobody makes them like you do.
- Yay.

26
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.366
- Hey, I want one.
- I’ll get the tea.

27
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:29.466
Huh?

28
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:33.033
Macaroons and tea make the perfect combination.

29
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.633
- Okay, let’s try them.
- Ah.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.933
Huh?

31
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.133
- What? It’s empty.
- Excuse me! What was that?

32
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.566
- Huh? No.
- Oh, man.

33
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:44.766
That’s so weird. Could I have dropped them?

34
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.066
I hope not.

35
00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.933
Huh? Hey, Chespin. Did you take all the macaroons again?

36
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.733
Ches! Chespin!

37
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.833
- Huh? You can’t eat them all.
- Ches! Ches! Ches!

38
00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.433
Come on!

39
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.800
Ches! Ches! Ches! Chespin!

40
00:02:02.966 --> 00:02:05.933
That was the last macaroon!

41
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.900
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

42
00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:12.466
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

43
00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:15.366
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

44
00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:18.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

45
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.066
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

46
00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:24.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

47
00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:27.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

48
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

49
00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:32.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

50
00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:35.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon ♪

51
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.933
On behalf of Chespin, I sincerely apologize.

52
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.366
Forget it.

53
00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:52.433
Yeah. It’s really not that big of a deal.

54
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.166
Maybe, but I really wanted a macaroon.

55
00:02:56.233 --> 00:02:58.666
Don’t worry. I can always make more.

56
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.233
Okay, now that we’re all set, how about a Pokémon battle?

57
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.933
Sounds good to me.

58
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.666
Hey, Chespin, let’s battle and get a little exercise.

59
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:12.733
Ches! Pin! Pin!

60
00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:16.266
- Let’s go, Froakie.
- Fro.

61
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:21.066
- Chespin, now it’s your time to shine!
- Pin, Chespin!

62
00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.600
Froakie, use Bubble!

63
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:24.566
Froakie!

64
00:03:24.633 --> 00:03:26.900
Dodge! Huh?

65
00:03:26.966 --> 00:03:31.900
- Chespin’s usually much faster than that.
- I think its tummy’s full.

66
00:03:31.966 --> 00:03:35.733
- Now, Chespin, use Tackle.
- Ches! Pin!

67
00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:39.266
-Okay, Froakie. Use Pound.

68
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:42.966
- Fro!
- Dodge it, Chespin.

69
00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.133
- Faster! Move!
- Pin! Pin!

70
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.600
Che? Che?

71
00:03:50.266 --> 00:03:52.766
Chespin!

72
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:54.366
Oh, well.

73
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.366
- Stop. That’s it.
- Pika.

74
00:03:57.433 --> 00:03:59.600
Guess I won but...

75
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:01.733
Froakie! Kie!

76
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.033
Being a Gym Leader and losing like that is kind of embarrassing.

77
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.500
The way things are now, I bet even Dedenne could beat Chespin in a battle.

78
00:04:10.566 --> 00:04:12.866
- Ne! Ne!
- No way!

79
00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:16.933
- I don’t think that would ever happen.
- Yeah? Prove it. Battle us.

80
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.733
Yeah. I want to see that.

81
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.666
What do you say, Chespin?

82
00:04:20.733 --> 00:04:22.400
Chespin! Pin!

83
00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:24.633
Ne! ne!

84
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.266
- Dedenne, show them what you can do.
- Denne.

85
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:31.166
Are you ready, Chespin? Now, don’t be overconfident,

86
00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:33.766
just because your opponent happens to be smaller than you.

87
00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:37.933
- Che! Chespin!
- Wow, I wonder if Chespin can handle this.

88
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.266
- Its stomach looks pretty full.
- Pikachu.

89
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:44.033
Now, this time we’ll go first. Use Tackle.

90
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.266
Che!

91
00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.366
Chespin!

92
00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:54.633
Ne! Ne! Dedenne!

93
00:04:58.866 --> 00:05:00.200
Oh!

94
00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.700
- You did it.
- Dedenne.

95
00:05:02.766 --> 00:05:05.766
And it looks like little sister comes out on top.

96
00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:08.700
Yeah, and big brother gets knocked down a notch or two.

97
00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:09.700
Pika.

98
00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.800
Look, look. Caterpie.

99
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.833
That’s great. Okay, my turn. Who?

100
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.833
Uh... I know! You’re a Swadloon.

101
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.066
- Exactly.
- Looks just like it.

102
00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.633
Dedenne.

103
00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.700
Okay, okay, how about this?

104
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:40.833
Okay, now, Chespin. I’m a Gym Leader and you’re my Pokémon, so here’s the deal.

105
00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.266
Chespin. Pin.

106
00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:46.433
We can’t have you battling like that just because you ate too much.

107
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.500
But not to worry, with this machine, you’ll be full of energy in no time.

108
00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.033
There. All done.

109
00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.600
We’ll get you moving again with my brand-new invention.

110
00:06:03.666 --> 00:06:09.200
Now, if this test run is successful, I’ll have Chespin use it.

111
00:06:09.266 --> 00:06:12.933
Okay, here goes. Exercise Gear on.

112
00:06:14.233 --> 00:06:16.700
I feel it.

113
00:06:16.766 --> 00:06:21.233
Treadmill accelerator speed... on.

114
00:06:22.266 --> 00:06:26.666
I can’t wait for Chespin to take a crack at this.

115
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.933
Uh! Uh! How do I stop this thing? Argh!

116
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.433
- Whoa, what was that?
- Black smoke.

117
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.666
- What happened?
- Pika!

118
00:06:47.733 --> 00:06:49.666
Oh, big brother?

119
00:06:49.733 --> 00:06:51.766
- What are you doing?
- Whoa, what is this?

120
00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:56.700
Well, it’s exercise gear designed to help get Chespin back into tip-top condition.

121
00:06:56.766 --> 00:06:59.700
- I don’t think it works.
- Ne! Ne!

122
00:06:59.766 --> 00:07:02.300
This will only take a second to repair

123
00:07:02.366 --> 00:07:05.266
so why don’t you give my invention a try, Chespin?

124
00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:07.933
Hey, I don’t see Chespin anywhere.

125
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.100
I know Chespin was here just a minute ago.

126
00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:14.533
It could’ve gotten frightened by the explosion and gone to hide.

127
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.333
Well, it couldn’t have gotten far.

128
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.833
Hey! Hey, Chespin!

129
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:23.600
- Chespin, where are you?
- Pika! Pika!

130
00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.400
Ches!

131
00:07:32.466 --> 00:07:34.933
Chespin, can you hear us?

132
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.900
I sure hope we find it soon.

133
00:07:36.966 --> 00:07:40.366
Gee, maybe Chespin doesn’t like us anymore?

134
00:07:40.433 --> 00:07:42.133
Huh? Oh!

135
00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.900
Don’t worry. We’re going to find Chespin.

136
00:07:44.966 --> 00:07:47.633
We just going to have to widen our search a bit.

137
00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.633
- Okay, let’s go.
- Pikachu!

138
00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.633
Chespin. Chespin.

139
00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.633
Oh my! What a cute little Chespin.

140
00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.233
But what are you doing here, I wonder.

141
00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.900
- Hey. Chespin.
- Pika!

142
00:08:14.966 --> 00:08:18.633
I’m starting to get really worried.

143
00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.266
I wonder if Chespin was really shocked after losing so bad.

144
00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:26.433
It’s my fault. I was the one who forced Chespin to have a battle

145
00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:30.766
after it had eaten all of those macaroons and now it doesn’t like me anymore.

146
00:08:30.833 --> 00:08:33.833
Chespin must have run away. I know it.

147
00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.799
I’m sure that’s not true.

148
00:08:35.866 --> 00:08:39.000
Maybe. I really hope you’re right.

149
00:08:39.066 --> 00:08:42.566
Let’s all split up and search the whole area.

150
00:08:42.633 --> 00:08:45.433
Yeah! Pikachu and I will go look over there.

151
00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.500
- Come on, buddy.
- Pikachu!

152
00:08:47.566 --> 00:08:49.533
We’ll come back here when we find Chespin.

153
00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.966
- Okay, I'm going to look over this way.
- Me, too!

154
00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:56.400
Hm. Then I’ll go this direction and take a look.

155
00:08:57.166 --> 00:09:00.433
Chespin. Chespin. Ches...

156
00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.233
Oh! Ches...

157
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.333
Chespin!

158
00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.833
- Huh? So, you’re awake, eh?
- Chespin! Chespin! Chespin!

159
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.833
I’ve just baked some delicious macaroons.

160
00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.600
Ches! Ches! Ches!

161
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.900
Huh? Huh?

162
00:09:20.833 --> 00:09:23.966
Mm! Ches! Ches! Mm! Mm! Ches!

163
00:09:24.033 --> 00:09:26.033
It’s Chespin.

164
00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.933
So, dear, do you like the macaroons I've baked?

165
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.666
- Chespin!
- Why, that’s just wonderful.

166
00:09:32.733 --> 00:09:37.666
- You may eat as many as you like.
- Chespin! Chem!

167
00:09:39.833 --> 00:09:42.133
It looks so happy.

168
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.533
Who’s that Pokémon?

169
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.300
It’s Delphox.

170
00:10:14.766 --> 00:10:18.133
- Find it?
- No, I didn’t see Chespin anywhere.

171
00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.133
- Pika.
- Me neither.

172
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:24.433
I can’t believe Chespin would have run away from us.

173
00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.466
Hey, Clemont. Any news about Chespin?

174
00:10:27.533 --> 00:10:29.433
Yeah, I found it.

175
00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.800
- Wow, that’s great.
- Pika!

176
00:10:31.866 --> 00:10:34.933
Thank goodness. So, why isn’t Chespin with you?

177
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.700
Doesn’t matter. I left Chespin where it was.

178
00:10:37.766 --> 00:10:41.066
- But why? Why would you leave Chespin?
- Ne! Ne?

179
00:10:41.133 --> 00:10:44.300
Well, it was at a kind-looking old woman’s house

180
00:10:44.366 --> 00:10:47.066
and Chespin looked really happy.

181
00:10:47.133 --> 00:10:49.466
- You’re kidding.
- What are you talking about?

182
00:10:49.533 --> 00:10:54.466
Well, I don’t think Chespin cares about me anymore.

183
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.933
Eating my macaroons seems to make you very happy.

184
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.066
- Chespin!
- I’m glad you enjoy them so much.

185
00:11:02.133 --> 00:11:04.600
- Chespin!
- Hey there.

186
00:11:04.666 --> 00:11:06.666
- Huh?
- Chespin?

187
00:11:06.733 --> 00:11:10.300
- Well, it looks like Wylie’s come back.
- Eh?

188
00:11:10.366 --> 00:11:12.833
Home again, home again.

189
00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:17.033
I was just thinking there’s something you can do for me.

190
00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.400
Ches!

191
00:11:20.466 --> 00:11:24.400
I won the village tournament.

192
00:11:24.466 --> 00:11:26.933
Boy, am I hungry.

193
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.966
Grandma, where are you? Oh, those look good.

194
00:11:30.033 --> 00:11:33.700
Just a minute. You can’t touch these macaroons yet.

195
00:11:33.766 --> 00:11:36.366
- Why not?
- Not one single bite

196
00:11:36.433 --> 00:11:38.133
until you have a battle with me.

197
00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:44.300
A battle again? You should know by now there’s no way you’re going to beat me.

198
00:11:44.366 --> 00:11:49.133
Wait. Maybe you found a Pokémon you think can win against my Delphox?

199
00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.133
That’s right! I’ve got a secret weapon today.

200
00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:53.966
Meet Chespin!

201
00:11:54.033 --> 00:11:56.366
Che? Che? Che?

202
00:11:56.433 --> 00:12:00.166
Huh! Grass type, eh? That’s just fine.

203
00:12:00.233 --> 00:12:06.333
On one condition. If I win, you’ll forgive me, for what I said yesterday.

204
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.666
All right, but if I win, then you’ll have to apologize to me.

205
00:12:12.666 --> 00:12:18.033
Now, today is going to be the day that I finally defeat you in a Pokémon battle.

206
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.466
- All right, Chespin.
- Chespin! Chespin!

207
00:12:20.533 --> 00:12:23.466
Right. Here we go, Delphox. Come on out.

208
00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.433
Will-O-Wisp.

209
00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.833
- Huh?
- What’s that?

210
00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.866
It’s coming from the house.

211
00:12:41.933 --> 00:12:44.100
- Oh, no. Chespin!
- Clemont!

212
00:12:44.166 --> 00:12:47.666
Looks to me like Clemont still cares about Chespin an awful lot.

213
00:12:47.733 --> 00:12:50.333
- Come on, let’s go, too.
- Pika!

214
00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.333
Chespin!

215
00:12:53.333 --> 00:12:54.866
Oh, Chespin, no!

216
00:12:54.933 --> 00:12:57.866
Chespin! Chespin! Ches!

217
00:12:57.933 --> 00:13:00.133
Ah!

218
00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.633
Please, little Chespin. Stay strong.

219
00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:09.433
- Quick, do something. Counterattack.
- Chespin! Chespin!

220
00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:14.433
Looks like it’s going to be another win for me!

221
00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.933
Dear, I guess little Chespin doesn’t know how to battle after all.

222
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.700
- What’s Chespin doing?
- It’s having a battle.

223
00:13:21.766 --> 00:13:24.666
- Shouldn’t we stop it?
- Who’s that Pokémon?

224
00:13:25.666 --> 00:13:30.166
Delphox, the Fox Pokémon and the final evolved form of Fennekin.

225
00:13:30.233 --> 00:13:33.366
When Delphox stares into the flame on the tip of its branch to achieve

226
00:13:33.433 --> 00:13:37.666
a focused state, it creates a white-hot spiral of fire with its psychic power.

227
00:13:37.733 --> 00:13:39.100
This isn’t good.

228
00:13:39.166 --> 00:13:43.000
A Fire type like Delphox puts a Grass type like Chespin at a disadvantage.

229
00:13:43.066 --> 00:13:45.866
- Sure does.
- Clemont, you’ve got to do something.

230
00:13:45.933 --> 00:13:49.566
But what? I know Chespin doesn’t like me anymore.

231
00:13:49.633 --> 00:13:52.033
It’s time to wrap this thing up.

232
00:13:53.633 --> 00:13:55.700
Delphox, Flamethrower.

233
00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:00.833
- Quick, Pikachu. Go help Chespin now.
- Pika!

234
00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.266
Chespin!

235
00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.100
Pin? Che?

236
00:14:08.166 --> 00:14:13.100
Oh! Stop it, Delphox! Stop it now. Stop it!

237
00:14:13.166 --> 00:14:16.900
Chespin. Are you all right?

238
00:14:16.966 --> 00:14:18.100
Pin! Chespin!

239
00:14:18.166 --> 00:14:20.333
- Clemont.
- I’m sorry.

240
00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.100
You see, Chespin is my Pokémon.

241
00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:27.100
Well, what do you know. It looks like I’ve made quite a mistake.

242
00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:31.366
Then, that’s that. I suppose that would make me the winner again.

243
00:14:31.433 --> 00:14:33.600
Oh!

244
00:14:33.666 --> 00:14:37.233
Che! Ches!

245
00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:39.300
- Chespin?
- Chespin!

246
00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:46.233
Hm. Chespin and I would like to finish the battle for you, ma’am, please.

247
00:14:47.233 --> 00:14:49.933
I’m going to think about Chespin’s feelings more.

248
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.233
By doing that, somehow I think it will help me grow as a person and a Trainer.

249
00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:56.600
Not sure what you mean by that,

250
00:14:56.666 --> 00:14:59.666
but anyway, I’d be pleased to let you battle for me

251
00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:02.700
and I’d be more pleased if you win.

252
00:15:02.766 --> 00:15:06.300
- That old man owes me an apology, got it?
- Huh?

253
00:15:06.366 --> 00:15:09.366
Wylie, that’s okay with you, isn’t it?

254
00:15:09.433 --> 00:15:12.800
Uh, okay. If that’s how the boy feels.

255
00:15:12.866 --> 00:15:16.400
Thank you very much. You ready to go, Chespin?

256
00:15:16.466 --> 00:15:17.700
Che.

257
00:15:17.766 --> 00:15:20.533
Chespin sure looks like it means business now.

258
00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:21.833
Pika!

259
00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.066
I don’t think Clemont’s feeling down anymore.

260
00:15:24.133 --> 00:15:27.166
- All right. You can do it, you two.
- Ne! Ne!

261
00:15:29.266 --> 00:15:31.400
Here we go then, battle begin!

262
00:15:31.466 --> 00:15:33.200
Will-O-Wisp.

263
00:15:36.433 --> 00:15:39.233
Now, Chespin, dodge by rolling!

264
00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.500
Chespin!

265
00:15:40.566 --> 00:15:43.900
It’s no good making Chespin attack with a full stomach,

266
00:15:43.966 --> 00:15:47.266
but if it can keep moving and stay out of the way...

267
00:15:47.333 --> 00:15:48.433
Che!

268
00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:52.166
Delphox, use Flamethrower!

269
00:15:52.233 --> 00:15:57.200
- All right, Chespin, drop and roll!
- Ches! Pin! Ches!

270
00:15:57.266 --> 00:16:01.433
I don’t know! Chespin just keeps rolling. Oh! Oh!

271
00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.866
Is his strategy working? It’s really hard to tell.

272
00:16:04.933 --> 00:16:08.833
I’m starting to think that it is. Being rounder helps it to roll around.

273
00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.833
Oh, yeah. Maybe that’ll keep Chespin from getting hit.

274
00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.200
Will-O-Wisp!

275
00:16:15.266 --> 00:16:19.033
- Chespin, keep rolling and dodging!
- Chespin!

276
00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:22.900
Wow, it is working! Now Chespin’s starting to move faster and faster!

277
00:16:22.966 --> 00:16:24.500
Yay, Chespin, way to go!

278
00:16:24.566 --> 00:16:27.266
- Chespin, feeling good?
- Chespin!

279
00:16:27.333 --> 00:16:31.166
- Use Tackle.
- Pin! Pin!

280
00:16:31.233 --> 00:16:33.200
Ches!

281
00:16:33.266 --> 00:16:36.366
All right. Now Chespin’s moving like its regular self!

282
00:16:36.433 --> 00:16:37.666
-Ches!

283
00:16:37.733 --> 00:16:43.300
- Let’s keep it up. Use Vine Whip!
- Pin! Chespin!

284
00:16:43.366 --> 00:16:46.033
- That won’t work on us.
- Huh, oh, no.

285
00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.500
Use Flamethrower!

286
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.400
Oh, Chespin!

287
00:16:55.466 --> 00:16:58.666
Oh!

288
00:17:00.666 --> 00:17:05.000
Please, Chespin. You’ve just got to get up. I believe in you!

289
00:17:05.066 --> 00:17:07.733
-Get up. You can do it.

290
00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.533
- What’s that?
- Pika!

291
00:17:15.599 --> 00:17:18.533
Overgrow. Chespin’s Special Ability!

292
00:17:18.599 --> 00:17:22.099
When Chespin’s in bad shape, its Grass-type moves get stronger.

293
00:17:22.166 --> 00:17:23.566
-Chespin!

294
00:17:23.633 --> 00:17:27.300
- Yes! It’s time to really show them.
- Chespin!

295
00:17:27.366 --> 00:17:32.000
- Vine Whip, let’s go!
- Pin! Pin! Chespin!

296
00:17:32.066 --> 00:17:35.400
Oh!

297
00:17:35.466 --> 00:17:38.400
- Great. That’s the way to do it.
- Pin! Pin!

298
00:17:38.466 --> 00:17:41.200
I’ve still got a trick or two up my sleeve.

299
00:17:41.266 --> 00:17:45.666
I didn’t think I’d need to use this, but I’m going to and that’ll be that!

300
00:17:45.733 --> 00:17:48.400
But, Wylie, you’re going to use that move?

301
00:17:48.466 --> 00:17:51.366
It’s much too dangerous to use and you know it!

302
00:17:51.433 --> 00:17:55.100
Now, you be quiet! There’s no going back now.

303
00:17:55.166 --> 00:17:58.966
Huh? Sounds like a super-strong move that could hurt the Pokémon who uses it.

304
00:17:59.033 --> 00:18:00.100
Pika!

305
00:18:00.166 --> 00:18:01.933
- Heads up.
- Chespin.

306
00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.333
Now, Mystical Fi...

307
00:18:07.466 --> 00:18:11.333
My, my, my back!

308
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.566
- Huh? Sir, are you all right?
- Ches? Chespin?

309
00:18:14.633 --> 00:18:20.066
Oh, dear. Now, didn’t I tell you you’d hurt yourself, Wylie? Poor thing!

310
00:18:20.133 --> 00:18:23.633
I see. She meant Wylie’d get hurt, not the Pokémon.

311
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.066
Pika!

312
00:18:25.133 --> 00:18:29.333
I’d say that’s enough battling for one day, Wylie.

313
00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.533
Heh! I guess I'll let you have this victory.

314
00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.533
Well, I suppose we should just call it a draw.

315
00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:40.266
I’m really sorry that we ended up dragging all of you nice folks

316
00:18:40.333 --> 00:18:42.233
into our little family squabble.

317
00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.066
We had a fight yesterday.

318
00:18:45.633 --> 00:18:48.566
Really going after that soup, aren’t you?

319
00:18:48.633 --> 00:18:53.333
What do you mean by that? Are you insinuating that I’m eating too much?

320
00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:57.100
Nope. I’m just saying a little restraint’s healthy.

321
00:18:57.166 --> 00:19:00.666
Oh, yeah? Well, there’ll be no dinner for you tonight.

322
00:19:00.733 --> 00:19:03.666
Hey! Come on!

323
00:19:06.666 --> 00:19:09.500
Oh! What’s that?

324
00:19:09.566 --> 00:19:11.866
Well, you see...

325
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.600
I bought it for you with the hopes that we could make up.

326
00:19:16.666 --> 00:19:19.366
Wylie! Now, isn’t that sweet?

327
00:19:19.433 --> 00:19:24.800
I bet you were going to apologize whether I won or lost, weren’t you?

328
00:19:24.866 --> 00:19:27.066
Course I was.

329
00:19:27.133 --> 00:19:31.833
Well, then, I think we should all eat Wylie’s apology. What do you say?

330
00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.200
- Huh!
- Really?

331
00:19:33.266 --> 00:19:35.200
- All right!
- Delish.

332
00:19:35.266 --> 00:19:36.500
Yay!

333
00:19:39.066 --> 00:19:42.066
Chespin, dear, I can’t thank you enough.

334
00:19:42.133 --> 00:19:45.300
I’d say you’re a very lucky Pokémon to have teamed up

335
00:19:45.366 --> 00:19:48.133
- with such a good and caring Trainer.
- Che!

336
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.900
So you didn’t run away, because you don’t like me?

337
00:19:50.966 --> 00:19:52.566
Chespin!

338
00:19:53.566 --> 00:19:56.566
Wow! You do. You like me, Chespin.

339
00:19:56.633 --> 00:19:59.633
Clemont, looks to me like you imagined the whole thing.

340
00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.166
I could tell how much Chespin cares about you

341
00:20:02.233 --> 00:20:04.333
by watching the two of you in that battle.

342
00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.766
- Oh, yeah. You were great.
- Ne! Ne! Ne! Ne!

343
00:20:07.833 --> 00:20:11.833
You’re my special partner. I hope you and I can be friends forever.

344
00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.166
Chespin!

345
00:20:13.233 --> 00:20:15.166
Thanks for everything.

346
00:20:15.233 --> 00:20:17.200
Come back anytime.

347
00:20:17.266 --> 00:20:19.366
- Right.
- Pin.

348
00:20:19.433 --> 00:20:22.233
And so, a brief misunderstanding has helped

349
00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.900
Clemont and Chespin strengthen the bond between them.

350
00:20:24.966 --> 00:20:28.500
Another happy ending in our heroes, many exciting adventures,

351
00:20:28.566 --> 00:20:31.033
as the journey continues.

352
00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.600
- It looks like it’s getting dark.
- Pika.

353
00:20:36.666 --> 00:20:40.766
Yeah, it doesn’t look like we’ll get to the Pokémon Center tonight either.

354
00:20:40.833 --> 00:20:43.866
I have an idea. Let’s just camp out!

355
00:20:43.933 --> 00:20:45.966
I thought of some great new imitations.
